		{
			dependencies: ["5E780FBECE1F61E6"]
			description: [
				"Schematics are the &9\"blueprint\"&r of a building, a map of where each block goes."
				"&6Create&r offers methods to create and deploy schematics."
				""
				"To begin, acquire a &bschematic and quill&r, then select two opposite corners to mark the area of the building you want to make a schematic of."
				"This area can be manually fine-tuned afterwards."
				""
				"After the selection area is at the correct size, use the &bschematic and quill&r again to name your schematic and save it."
				""
				"&dYou can do this in a separate world to bring in a building you made or found. (We won't judge)"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"After saving the schematic, grab an &bempty schematic&r and a &6schematic table&r."
				""
				"Opening the &6schematic table&r, you can see a list of all saved schematics."
				"Adding the &bempty schematic&r and selecting a schematic will write it down, giving you a &bfilled schematic&r."
				""
				"Afterwards, head to where you want to place down the schematic, and use the &bschematic item&r to place a &d\"ghost\"&r of your building."
				"After fine-tuning the position, you can &6finally go ahead and start manually placing blocks one by one.&r"
				""
				"&a...just kidding!&r Well, you CAN do that, but there's ways to &2automate&r this process."
			]
			icon: "create:schematic_and_quill"
			id: "570E5A9796C52276"
			rewards: [{
