		{
			dependencies: ["08D3D407B57B7B3B"]
			description: [
				"&6[W] To Ponder!&r"
				""
				"&6Trains&r are great for long range transportation and logistics."
				"&eBut what about normal minecart tracks?&r"
				""
				"The &6cart assembler&r lets you build a contraption &eon top of a minecart&r"
				""
				"To use it, place it on a minecart track, then build the contraption on top of it."
				"&aRemember to glue it all up!&r"
				""
				"To assemble the contraption, place a &7minecart&r inside, and apply a &credstone&r signal to the assembler."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To disassemble the contraption, &cpunch out&r the &7minecart,&r or have it ride over an &cUNPOWERED&r assembler."
				""
				"By using a &6wrench,&r a &6cart contraption&r can be &apicked up, and placed back down elsewhere&r. &cHaving certain blocks on board will disallow picking up the contraption &4AT ALL.&r &c(Like mob spawners)&r"
				"&3These blocks can still be moved by moving the minecart normally."
				""
				"Overall, &6cart contraptions&r are great for farms where the circular rotation of a &6mechanical bearing&r &edoesn't quite cut it&r, or setups arranged in a straight line."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&dTip:&r A &6mechanical plough&r can &epick up rails&r., while a &6deployer&r &ecan place them&r."
				""
				""
				"{ \"text\": \"The two could be combined into one contraption...\", \"underlined\": \"true\", \"hoverEvent\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"There's a video URL here...\"}, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ss8LtGKxCx8\" } }"
			]
