			title: "Item Type Hell"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0D97FCEA76ACC0D1"]
			description: [
				"Storage buses act as a way to link an &bexternal inventory&r such as a &nchest, package,&r or &nvault&r to your ae2 system such that you can access the items."
				""
				"Storage buses also have a few &aunique tricks&r such as allowing &npriority designation, filtering,&r and even &noverflow automation&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To set priority simply click the &atop right&r of the UI:"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_inv_ui.png width:153 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"And select a &anumber&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_pri_ui.png width:141 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"&bHigher numbers&r go &n\"first\"&r and will attempt to put items &ointo&r the inventory first and &oextract&r &nlast&r."
				""
				"&dLower numbers&r &cinvert&r this behavior."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Filtering can be done by simply dragging an item from your &ninventory&r or &nJEI&r into a slot in the UI."
				""
				"This will filter what items/fluids the storage bus is &eallowed to interact&r with &7unsurprisingly I imagine&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Adding an &cInverter Card&r to the upgrade slot will &nflip&r this behavior to allow interaction with &aeverything&r &oexcept&r what is listed in the filter."
				""
				"Adding a &6Fuzzy Card&r will allow you to toggle if the storage bus treats &asame items&r of &cdifferent durability&r or &cnbt&r as the same thing or not."
				""
				"A major use-case for fuzzy cards being handling items from mob farms such as tools or armor."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Adding an &4Overflow Card&r will void excess items automatically."
				""
				"This can be an easy way to &cdelete&r vast amounts of items &nby accident&r if the storage bus is &cimproperly configured&r since, if your drives are full, all new inputs will be &cdeleted forever&r."
				""
				"There is also the issue of &epollution&r when destroying things..."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&6Capacity cards&r are... a thing that exists."
				""
				"You can filter more things. Thats it yeah."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As if the storage bus couldn't already do a lot of things, the buttons on the &a← left side ←&r of the UI have unique functionality as well!"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&dPartition storage&r shown as the &nwrench icon&r is able to set the filters on the bus by looking at what is already in the inventory."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_partition.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&dReport Inaccessable Items&r is a toggle between &nyes/no&r that lets you choose whether or not items existing in an inventory not part of the filter can still be seen by the network."
				""
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_report_no.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/strorage_bus_report_yes.png width:185 height:79 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&dFiltered Operations&r is a toggle between:"
				""
				"&nFilter on import and export&r "
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_filter__both.png width:185 height:100 align:center} "
				""
				"&nFilter only on import&r"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_filter_out.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"And finally the &dInput Output Mode&r."
				"This toggles between:"
				""
				"&nBi-directional&r"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_io_bi.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"&nInsert only&r"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_io_insert.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"&nExtract only&r"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/storage_bus_io_extract.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
			]
			id: "5CD2858BBC7FAF3A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3F71F6E733E77645"
				item: "nyagibits_bytes:tier_one_strawberry"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "No not like that! Get your mind out of the gutter"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1E560294F6CE7C6A"
				item: "ae2:storage_bus"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Exposing your Inventories"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 8.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"5CD2858BBC7FAF3A"
				"0BCC4B5B144C4EFA"
			]
			description: [
				"As if storage buses didn't do enough already they have yet another &aunique and very powerful&r interaction with &6interfaces&r."
				""
				"&cS&6u&eb&an&be&dt&cs&r!"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/subnetting.png width:177 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/subnetting.png width:177 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Pictured here we have two networks. "
				"&bBlue&r and &cRed&r."
				""
				"&bBlue&r is connected via a &astorage bus&r to an interface on the &cRed&r network. The networks themselves are seperated and only bridged by a &6quartz fiber&r &7(power only)&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In this example the &bBlue&r network is able to see that the &cRed&r network has a drive and is able to pull from that inventory."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/subnetting.png width:177 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"The &cRed&r network in this instance is unable to see the &bBlue&r network, since this subnet interaction is 1 way."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This mechanic has many use-cases. A primary one is &nexpanding how much 1 channel is able to do&r from the main controller to a nearly &6infinite&r amount. "
				""
				"Instead of a direct connection from the master controller, &na single channel&r can be used to subnet into another system &adedicated to a process&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This also means subnets can &6endlessly chain&r into more subnets."
				""
