		{
			dependencies: ["5453F57FB425DD00"]
			description: [
				"&dP2P Tunnels&r also known as &nPoint-to-Point Tunnels&r are a way to shuttle various things an &aarbitrarily long distance&r through your network."
				""
				"For this quest the usecase will focus on &credstone signaling&r but it is worth noting that p2p tunnels can work with many different &b\"substances\"&r. "
				""
				"&7Attachment types can be viewed by clicking the p2p in the quest above and looking for the JEI entry &n[P2P Tunnel Attunement]&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&lSo why care about p2p redstone?&r"
				""
				"Bases here tend to &eswell in size&r very very quickly, and many &abiome-specific interactions&r will cause sprawling infrastructure many &dhundreds or thousands of blocks&r from the centralized area."
				""
				"Create's redstone link has a &crange limit&r of &n256 blocks in radius&r. Which, while usually fine for bases, &cwon't be enough long term&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In this example we will simply be pointing a &dlevel emitter&r into a &bp2p tunnel on the &n← left ←&r with the other side of the &6tunnel off to the &n→ right →&r. "
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"This distance can be &aarbitrarily long&r or even &athrough quantum rings&r. But for the sake of the diagram, it is nearby."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"By default a placed p2p tunnel will be attuned to connect to &nae2 cables&r. "
				""
				"To change this to &credstone attunement&r, simply &nright click&r the p2p tunnel with any listed item under the &aredstone-attunement-forge-tag&r as seen on the &nfollowing pages&r or in JEI."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone_tag_one.png width:130 height:185 align:center}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone_tag_two.png width:130 height:185 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone_tag_three.png width:130 height:185 align:center}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone_tag_four.png width:130 height:185 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_redstone_tag_five.png width:130 height:185 align:center}"
				""
				"&6Note:&r This tag list is significantly expanded from base Ae2 and is subject to updates."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"With that out of the way let's actually &ouse&r these tunnels!"
				""
				"You'll want to place &62&r P2P tunnels onto an ME cable line and &nattune&r them to redstone signals"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"&7Their exact positions does not matter but they &l&n&amust&r &7exist on the same network. P2P tunnels also &c&nwill not function&r &7between subnets."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"By default the tunnels &cdon't know to talk to each other&r. To link them together you'll use a &bmemory card&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"To use the memory card simply &nshift + right-click&r the side of the tunnel you wish to be the &ainput&r. &7More on this later&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"When you do this you will see a &npopup&r letting you know a new configuration has been &acreated and copied&r to the memory card. You will also see a visual update on the &ncard and tunnel&r showing the frequency that has been copied."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_four.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"You can also see above on the \"what am I looking at\" overlay that the tunnel itself has a frequency listed. Here it is &l0&a5&8F&e4&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_jade.png width:185 height:78 align:center}"
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_five.png width:185 height:67 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To designate an &coutput&r side simply &nright-click&r another tunnel."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_three.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Something to note here. The redstone line &cdidn't instantly update&r. This will happen sometimes and requires the &ainput&r side to be updated to register properly."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"When &bproperly updated&r you now have a tunnel of redstone signal!"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_six.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"A fun feature of p2p tunnels is, despite only allowing 1 &ainput&r, you can have an &6arbitrary amount of &r&coutputs&r!"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_seven.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Another &efeature/limitation&r of p2p redstone is the fact that the tunnels are &emonodirectional&r in their signal sending. Meaning a side designated as &coutput&r can not send the signal backwards. &n&lOnly&r the &ainput&r side can send a signal through."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_memory_eight.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"An important note to make is that modded redstone items can often have &eweird and inconsistent behavior&r with p2p tunnels. It is &nvery important&r to test these interactions before planning out a build."
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/p2p_weird_connections.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
			]
			id: "4E29F03DB5A55935"
