			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["55D9685F3A80E054"]
			description: [
				"&cRed String&r blocks are a rather arcane and advanced way to interface with automation in your base."
				""
				"This set of blocks is able to link to blocks &6&nat range&r&r and interface with said blocks in different ways depending on the type of container bound."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"It is important to note that &cred string blocks&r &ncan not&r link to each other. This ironically ends up being a &aboon&r for them, more on this later."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"For the sake of the dioramas a &awand of the forest&r will be held in hand in order to render the &cred string connection&r to the example inventory/block."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cRed String Container&r is able to connect to inventories, &7such as a chest&r, and basically, &apretend to be that inventory&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_cont_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"In practice what that means is the &cred string container&r can now be the &binput/output&r of an inventory without the inventory itself being touched by hoppers or anything else."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Something interesting to note here is, if the &cred string container&r and chest &nboth&r have outputting hoppers, the &cdefault vanilla rules&r still apply."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_cont_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Pictured above, items will prioritize being exported &bbased on vanilla hopper rules due to the chest-side being a side input&r."
				""
				"If items are &abulk inserted&r into the chest directly, the items will even split between both outputs."
				""
				"&7Side note because redstone was invented by the devil, the output behavior can change on relog&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cred string container&r is also able to handle export/import with a wide variety of modded item logistics"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_cont_three.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cRed String Dispenser&r is a specialized version of the &cred string container&r that can ineract with &6dispensers&r and &6droppers&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_disp.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Besides item I/O, this block can &bactivate&r dispensers and dropped when it is powered. &aRemote activation&r!"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cRed String Comparator&r is able to take a &6comparator output&r of an attached inventory."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_comp.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"This comes in extra handy in those situations where every face of an inventory has something else in the way already."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cRed String Nutrifier&r is a bit of an odd-ball. This block is able to remotely &abonemeal&r crops."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_nutr_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Something important shown here is that the &cnutrifier&r is looking at the &bcrop&r and &nnot&r the &6farm-tile&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This may seem pretty useless but it is important to remember that various trees tend to not grow properly due to &eobscure directionality rules&r in the base game. In addition several modded trees have a tendancy to &coverride blocks&r as they grow."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_nutr_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"And so with some chaining with &cred string dispensers&r the actual grow-mechanism can be seperated from the crop. &4I wonder if anything especially hazardous would need this later on&r..."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &cRed String Spoofer&r is quite a bit more involved than the other red string components. So much so half of this questline is just the &cspoofer&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_spoof_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"In short the spoofer can &atransfer the effects&r of a flower onto another flower or mushroom."
				""
				"Above you can see a &bmarimorphosis petite&r spoofed onto a &6mystical white flower&r."
				""
				"In practice however things get &ecomplicated&r... &7(this is your queue to turn the page)&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"A major thing to get out of the way is the fact that &efunctional or generating flowers&r &ncan not&r be &espoofed&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_spoof_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As shown below a flower &nthat is generating or functional&r will be &cignored&r by other spoofers and target a flower in front of them instead &7(if in range)&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_spoof_three.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"A great use-case initially for this is seperating &cdangerous parts&r of the flower automation from your &6oh-so-expensive flowers&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_entro_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Shown above an &bentropinnyum&r spoofed to a white flower. Here exploding tnt by the white flower will function &nexactly the same way&r as if the tnt went off by the &bentropinnyum&r itself."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Taking this up a notch, since spoofers &7(or red string containers in general)&r can't link to each other, you can &nline them up&r and attach multiple spoofers to the same flower since the spoofers ignore each other."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_entro_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Now seeing this a certain &6waterfowl&r may be tempted to ask... &l&n&cD&6o&ee&as &bI&dt &cS&6t&ea&ac&bk&r?"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"And the answer is, &6&oholy shit yes it does&r. Up to 8 blocks away &7(range limit of red string blocks)&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_goose.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Going back to the entropinnyums for a second. Yes &cdecay still works&r here as intended. Keep that in mind for your setups."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_entro_three.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As if spoofers didn't do enough. There is also "
				"&l&cM&6UL&eT&aI&bS&dP&cO&6O&eF&aI&bN&dG&r &e:thunder_sound_effect:&r"
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_multi_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"Seen above we have a white flower with &n2 different flowers spoofed&r onto it."
				""
				"A &bmarimorphosis petite&r and a &6rannuncarpus&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now this is admittedly a bad demonstration of the mechanic since the &6rannuncarpus&r doesn't spoof as anticipated. This is more to get the &dbrain juices&r moving."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_multi_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"And finally the weirdest red-string block, the &cRed String Interceptor&r."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_int_one.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"The interceptor basically works as a &nlong range observer&r, sending out a 1 tick pulse whenever a player interacts with a \"&esufficiently advanced block&r\"."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now here \"&esufficiently advanced block&r\" is a bit of a wider term than what typically fires an observer. Below we can see a &afurnace&r being bound to the interceptor &ndespite the fact&r that normally opening a furnace does not set off an observer."
				""
				"{image:compression:textures/quests/rs_int_two.png width:185 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"The use cases for the interceptor is much more limited but hey, you can do some &6insane hidden activation mechanisms &rwith it."
				""
				"&4Wonder who else thought about that..&r"
			]
